Found by the pre-release audit 2026-11-13 (fidelity-auditor; reproduced by the main agent).

One long-lived Environment with a cached FileSystemLoader -- what the Environment POD recommends -- still grows per render:
- plain template (for/if/set/filters): 0 kB/render
- A{% include "part.njk" %}B: 7.87 kB/render (3000 renders: RSS 23148 -> 46752 kB, main-agent probe at HEAD 1a9a608)
- 300 includes in a for loop: 1.4 MB/render; with a 2000-row context the whole context is kept (~730 kB per request)
- asyncEach over 20 items ~50 kB; each 'template not found' ~4.5 kB; include ignore missing of a missing template ~12 kB; noCache loader 4 kB/render (51 kB with one include)

Cause (auditor, each confirmed by a scratch patch that removes the leak): Environment.pm:464-478 waterfall and Lib.pm:391-401 / 427-438 async_iter / async_for close over the coderef held in $next -- a self-reference cycle per call. Port-only (JS has a tracing GC). Fix direction validated in scratch: __SUB__ (feature current_sub) instead of the captured $next; leak probes then measure 0 kB and the suite stays green.

Probe: one Environment, Loader::FileSystem(['views']), warm 200 renders, then render N times and compare VmRSS from /proc/self/status.

Done when: a regression test proves include / asyncEach / cache-miss renders free their Context (weaken + is-freed check, no new prereq), and the probes read 0 kB/render.

Release blocker: a long-running process (web app) grows without bound. skilletor (short-lived CLI, own loader) is not affected. See also the macro/Context cycle card and k96.

2026-11-17 main agent, re-diagnosed at HEAD 621ad19: cause confirmed. waterfall (Environment.pm:458) and Lib async_iter / async_for (Lib.pm:393, :429) do 'my $next; $next = sub { ... $next ... }' -- the closure holds itself and, through tasks and callback, the render's Context, Frame and Template. Count probe (weak refs on every Context / Frame / Template created, render_string x300): include, include ignore missing and asyncEach each leave 1 Context + 1 Frame + 1 Template per render; asyncAll leaves none. With __SUB__ in place of the captured $next (runtime monkeypatch, repo untouched) all three read 0. No design decision needed; ready for the worker.

